      "message": "AFAIK the rest of Skia has any way to bind up a uniform that\u0027s struct-typed. To the best of my knowledge, Ganesh and Graphite only support a hardcoded list of uniform types (via an enum), and user types are just not in the list. I don\u0027t know if this is something we would ever want or intend to support.\n\nIOW, if Skia could never bind the uniform to a value, we probably don\u0027t need to worry if the codegen is wrong. We might just be OK emitting an error in the frontend? @brianosman@google.com WDYT?\n\n(IMO even if Runtime Effects exposed binding a uniform struct, it\u0027d probably be easier to treat the struct as a bunch of individual variables from a uniform binding perspective, and paper over it in the frontend somehow)",
